    kind: invariant  # 4c3d
    title: "A docs-only PR selects only packages/*/tests/, so the 13 root-level gates that READ docs never run on the change class they exist to check (measured: #639 merged a measurement record that fails check-measurement-frame, CI green)"  # 4c3d
    status: violated  # 4c3d
    priority: 1  # 4c3d
    parent:  # 4c3d
    tags:  # 4c3d
    - ci_infrastructure  # 4c3d
    - docs  # 4c3d
    - analysis_quality  # 4c3d
    isbefore: []  # 4c3d
    duplicate_of: []  # 4c3d
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 4c3d
    pr_ref:  # 4c3d
    description: "FOUND 2026-08-30 while starting ADR-0049 step 3. `dev` was RED and had been\nsince PR #639 merged, on a test nobody could have seen fail.\n\nTHE OBSERVATION, run not reasoned:\n\n  $ python3 -m pytest tests/test_check_measurement_frame.py -q\n  FAILED TestTheLiveTree::test_the_shipped_records_pass\n    0009-deferred-crossing-reachability.md: no `## Frame` block (ADR-0048 A3)\n\nPR #639 added `docs/measurements/0009-*.md` with no `## Frame` block. ADR-0048\nA3 makes that block mandatory from 0009 onward and `scripts/check-measurement-frame`\nis the gate. CI passed the PR anyway.\n\nWHY IT PASSED, from the manifest #639 itself committed:\n\n  # Reason: no test-relevant files changed (docs/config only)\n  # Changed source files: 0\n  # Selected tests: 339        <- ALL under packages/*/tests/, NONE under tests/\n\n`smart-test` slices on `^packages/.*/src/.*\\.py$`. A docs-only change yields\nzero changed sources, and the docs/config fallback then selects the PACKAGE\nsuites only. The root suite is not selected.\n\nTHE INVERSION, which is the actual defect and not a coverage gap: the gates\nthat govern documents live in ROOT `tests/`. Thirteen of them read `docs/`:\n\n  test_check_measurement_frame       test_adr_readme_index_sync\n  test_adr_supersession_symmetry     test_concept_audit_record\n  test_generate_architecture_linker_inventory   test_generate_concepts\n  test_generate_security_md          test_generate_concept_axes\n  test_prepare_release_notes_promotion          test_ci_failover_retired\n  test_per_package_fallback          test_top_level_test_map  test_smart_test\n\nSo on the ONE change class these gates exist to check -- a PR that changes only\ndocuments -- the selector runs every test EXCEPT them. The fallback is not\nmerely incomplete; it is pointed the wrong way. An ADR-only PR likewise skips\nthe ADR supersession and index gates.\n\nI verified the other twelve are currently green (55 passed), so the live damage\nis one record. The exposure is not one record.\n\nREPRO\n  git checkout 4c82fe0131\n  python3 -m pytest tests/test_check_measurement_frame.py -q   # red\n  git show 4c82fe0131:.ci/affected-tests.txt | grep -c '^tests/'  # 0\n\nFIX SHAPE (structural, not a list): the docs/config fallback should select the\nroot suite, or -- better, because it does not decay -- the selector should map\nCHANGED DOC PATHS to the root tests that READ them, the way\n`top_level_test_map.py` already maps changed helpers to root tests. A hardcoded\n\"also run these 13\" list is the shape that rots (LIVE rule 10): the fourteenth\ndoc gate lands green and unrun.\n\nNOT THE SAME AS INV-sotam. That one is \"smart-test runs NOTHING and exits 0 on\na clean tree given explicit targets\". This one runs 339 tests and exits 0 while\nskipping the only ones that could fail.\n\nThe 0009 frame block is fixed forward in the same PR that files this; the\nselector is not, because changing test selection is a bigger change than a\nred-dev fix should carry."  # 4c3d
    fields:  # 4c3d
      statement: "Every gate that governs a document must run on the pull requests that change that document."  # 4c3d
      root_cause: "smart-test slices on ^packages/.*/src/.*\\.py$; a docs-only change yields zero changed sources and the docs/config fallback then selects the package suites only, never the root suite where all 13 doc-reading gates live."  # 4c3d
