- op: discuss  # f332
  at: '2026-08-30T05:54:38Z'  # f332
  by: agent  # f332
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f332
  clock: 3  # f332
  nonce: f332  # f332
  message: "SATISFIED by PR #642 (0ae66a5965), with behavioural evidence rather than a proxy.\n\nBEFORE, on a tree whose only edits were docs/ + CHANGELOG.md:\n  $ ./scripts/smart-test --manifest\n  Manifest written to .ci/affected-tests.txt (0 tests - no Python source changed)\n  # Reason: no test-relevant files changed (docs/config only)\n  # Selected tests: 0\nAnd the live consequence: tests/test_check_measurement_frame.py::TestTheLiveTree::test_the_shipped_records_pass was RED on dev and had been since PR #639 merged, because measurement 0009 shipped without the ## Frame block ADR-0048 A3 requires and no pull request could have run the gate.\n\nAFTER, same shape of change:\n  # Selected tests: 14   <- 13 doc gates + the smart-test suite\nAnd the item's own repro, re-run on the merged tree: PR #643 is docs-only and its committed manifest selects 13 root tests, all of which read docs/. 203 tests, 6 seconds.\n\nDERIVED, NOT LISTED, which is the half that matters for durability. The selection greps tests/test_*.py for a docs/ reference rather than naming today's thirteen, so the fourteenth doc gate is covered by the commit that adds it. A hardcoded roster is the shape that decayed F2_LANGS to nine of fifteen shipped catalogues.\n\nA CONTROL REFUTED MY OWN COMMENT. The union has three grep spellings and I wrote that each was load-bearing; the test asserting strict inequality FAILED -- 'docs/' alone reaches all thirteen today and the two quoted-bareword arms are defensive for a Path(\"docs\") spelling no root test uses. Comment and test both corrected to say that.\n\nONE LATENT BUG THE FIX MADE REACHABLE, fixed in the same PR: grep -c . prints 0 AND exits 1 on empty input, so || echo 0 fired in addition and wrote a bare 0 line into the manifest header. Unreachable before, because a change with zero source files exited at the docs/config-only branch and never reached that writer."  # f332
